<title>USA: Farmington, N.M., revs yld 6.45 pct in 2022.</title>
<headline>Farmington, N.M., revs yld 6.45 pct in 2022.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said it has tentatively priced $90 million Farmington, N.M., pollution control revenue refunding bonds, series 1997 Series D, at a top yield of 6.45 percent in 2022.  </p>
<p>City of Farmington, New Mexico</p>
<p>RE: $90,000,000*</p>
<p>% Pollution Control Revenue</p>
<p>Refunding Bonds, 1997 Series D</p>
<p>(Public Service Company of New Mexico San Juan Project)</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Ba1		   S&amp;P: BB+</p>
<p>		 EXPECTED		   EXPECTED</p>
<p>DATED: 02/21/1997</p>
<p>FIRST COUPON: 10/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 04/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>04/01/2022	     90,000M    6.45  %</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 04/01/2007    102.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 04/01/2009</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>The award is expected Tuesday, January 28, 1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on February 21, 1997.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>Citicorp Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. Incorporated</p>
<p>BancAmerica Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
